{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuarkState.PhotonPairNormalForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuarkState.PhotonPairNormalForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTraceOnHecke","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Mul","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Coeff"],"declarations":76,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.rho_delta_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.rho_delta_sq","kind":"theorem","line":605,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L605-L611","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.rho_delta_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.rho_delta_inv","kind":"theorem","line":596,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L596-L603","doc":"**The `(2,1)` channel cannot see a global flavour flip of `Δ = σ₀σ₁σ₀`.**\n`ρ(Δ⁻¹) = ρ(Δ)`, equivalently the full twist `Δ²` acts as `1` on `(2,1)`. So on\nthe alternating word, `uuu` and `ddd` have the same nucleon state, although the\nfull normal forms differ (`word010_hPart_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.gSplus_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.gSplus_one","kind":"theorem","line":587,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L587-L594","doc":"…and the `t¹` coefficient is nonzero: `g(1) = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.template_SplusAVG_proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.template_SplusAVG_proton","kind":"theorem","line":574,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L574-L585","doc":"**Order `t¹`: flavour is decided.** For the corpus template `S+ AVG` on the\nproton (shifts `0, −½, −½`) the `(2,1)` character is `(q − 1)·g(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.gSplus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.gSplus","kind":"def","line":567,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L567-L571","doc":"The cofactor `g(q) = (q+1)(q⁴+1)P(q)/(4q⁹)` of the corpus template. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.template_S0_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.template_S0_zero","kind":"theorem","line":557,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L557-L565","doc":"The flavour-blind template `S0` (all quark letters `σ`): character\nidentically `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.template_order_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.template_order_zero","kind":"theorem","line":546,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L546-L554","doc":"**Order `t⁰`: flavour is invisible.** At `q = 1` the `(2,1)` character of\nthe nucleon word is `0` for EVERY choice of quark shifts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.rho_letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.rho_letter","kind":"theorem","line":538,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L538-L544","doc":"A letter's `(2,1)` image IS the nucleon-word factor: evaluating `h` at\n`q − q⁻¹` and applying `ρ` to `σ_g + c·h·1` gives `lA`/`lB`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.nucleonStateOfQuarks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.nucleonStateOfQuarks","kind":"def","line":534,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L534-L536","doc":"The nucleon state built from three single-letter quark states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.nucleonState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.nucleonState","kind":"def","line":525,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L525-L532","doc":"**The nucleon state** (owner decision D2, 2026-11-15): the `(2,1)` image of\nthe core-plus-quarks word `(σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³ · ℓ₀(c₁) ℓ₀(c₂) ℓ₁(c₃)`. With\n`cᵢ = flavourShift εᵢ` it is built from three single-letter quark states\n(`nucleonStateOfQuarks`). The corpus `AVG` pair rule gives `c = −½`, which is\na pair AVERAGE and NOT a single letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.lB_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.lB_eq","kind":"theorem","line":522,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L522-L523","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.lA_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.lA_eq","kind":"theorem","line":520,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L520-L521","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.lB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.lB","kind":"def","line":517,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L517-L518","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.lA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.lA","kind":"def","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L513-L516","doc":"Template letters, written out entrywise: `ρ(σ₀) + c·h·1` and\n`ρ(σ₁) + c·h·1` with `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.rho_pairNF_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.rho_pairNF_split","kind":"theorem","line":497,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L497-L505","doc":"The γγ product's `(2,1)` image splits as the degree-0 scalar plus the\nquark state. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.pairChannelState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.pairChannelState","kind":"def","line":489,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L489-L495","doc":"The `(2,1)` projection of the word-degree ≥ 1 part of `NF(γ(φ)γ(ψ))`.\nThis was the agent's original \"quark state\" hypothesis. The owner RETIRED it as\nthe quark state on 2026-11-15 (D1/D2): at level 2 the `(2,1)` channel is a\nthree-strand, isospin-½, nucleon-type channel. It is kept under a neutral name\nbecause the theorems about it still hold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.rho_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.rho_unit","kind":"theorem","line":487,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L487-L487","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.rho_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.rho_mul","kind":"theorem","line":478,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L478-L485","doc":"**`ρ` is multiplicative** on the NF algebra at `h = q − q⁻¹`, so the\n`(2,1)` projection of a normal form is well defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.rho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.rho","kind":"def","line":473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L473-L476","doc":"`ρ` on the NF module, basis images `1, A, B, BA, AB, ABA`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.rB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.rB","kind":"def","line":470,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L470-L471","doc":"`ρ(σ₁)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.rA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.rA","kind":"def","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L468-L469","doc":"`ρ(σ₀)` in the reduced-Burau `(2,1)` representation of the probe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.word001_hPart_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.word001_hPart_one","kind":"theorem","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L451-L458","doc":"**The same-generator run on the builder word leaves only `c₁ + c₂`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.word001_formal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.word001_formal","kind":"theorem","line":444,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L444-L449","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.word010_hPart_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.word010_hPart_one","kind":"theorem","line":433,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L433-L442","doc":"**Per-letter readout on the alternating word.** With `h` formal, the `h¹`\npart is `(c₂, 0, 0, c₁, c₃, 0)`: each letter's bit sits on its own coordinate\n(the word with that letter deleted). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.word010_formal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.word010_formal","kind":"theorem","line":426,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L426-L431","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.word001_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.word001_eq","kind":"theorem","line":420,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L420-L424","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.word001","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.word001","kind":"def","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L416-L418","doc":"The builder-placement word `ℓ₀(c₁)ℓ₀(c₂)ℓ₁(c₃)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.word010_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.word010_eq","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L410-L414","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.word010","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.word010","kind":"def","line":406,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L406-L408","doc":"The alternating word `ℓ₀(c₁)ℓ₁(c₂)ℓ₀(c₃)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.sameGen_letters_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.sameGen_letters_commute","kind":"theorem","line":399,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L399-L404","doc":"Letters on the same generator commute: they lie in the commutative\nsubalgebra generated by `σ_g`. So flavour bits inside a same-generator run can\nonly be read as a multiset. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.letterH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.letterH","kind":"def","line":395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L395-L397","doc":"A letter with a general shift: `σ_g + c·h·1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.pairBar_netFlavour","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.pairBar_netFlavour","kind":"theorem","line":364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L364-L383","doc":"With the second photon flavour-flipped (`σ ↦ σ⁻¹` on its letters), the net\nflavour is `−(ψ₀ + ψ₁ + (φ₀ + φ₁)ψ₀₁)`. The flavour comes from the photon's own\nletters: it is an INPUT, not produced by the collision. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_three_letters_all_up","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_three_letters_all_up","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L350-L362","doc":"**(Q2) The nucleon flavours are not extractable from one photon pair.**\nWrite `NF(γγ)` as three letters plus any remainder of zero net flavour. Then all\nthree letters are `u`; `uud` and `udd` are impossible for every `(φ, ψ)`, so the\nset asked for is EMPTY. `CharZero` is used only to separate `−1, −2, −3` from `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_netFlavour","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_netFlavour","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L344-L348","doc":"The photon pair (both photons built from `σ` letters, `q`-independent labels)\nhas net flavour zero, for EVERY colour content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.letter_sum_flavour_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.letter_sum_flavour_swap","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L336-L342","doc":"**(Q3) Residual freedom.** Per-letter flavour is NOT recoverable from a sum\nof letters: `u` on `σ₀` plus `d` on `σ₁` is the same element as `d` on `σ₀`\nplus `u` on `σ₁`. Only the net flavour is determined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.netFlavour_letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.netFlavour_letter","kind":"theorem","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L331-L334","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.netFlavour_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.netFlavour_add","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L327-L329","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.netFlavour","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.netFlavour","kind":"def","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L324-L325","doc":"Net flavour: the `h¹` coefficient on the unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.hPart_one_pairNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.hPart_one_pairNF","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L309-L315","doc":"The `h¹` part of the photon pair product is `N₁`, now as a statement about\nthe formal variable (the labels are constants `C aᵢ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_formal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_formal","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L301-L307","doc":"The `h¹` part of the photon pair product is `N₁`, now as a statement about\nthe formal variable (labels are constants `C aᵢ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.quarkLetter_flavour_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.quarkLetter_flavour_difference","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L293-L299","doc":"The two flavours of a letter differ by exactly `−h·1`: `σ⁻¹ − σ = −h`. The\ndifference is purely order `h¹` and sits in word degree 0. (The bar involution\n`q ↦ q⁻¹` sends `h ↦ −h`; a bar-parity statement about the quark state is NOT\nproved here.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.quarkState_flavour_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.quarkState_flavour_ne","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L287-L291","doc":"The quark state distinguishes the flavours (non-vacuity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.quarkLetter_order_ge_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.quarkLetter_order_ge_two","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L277-L285","doc":"Orders `≥ 2` vanish: a letter is exactly affine in `h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.quarkState_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.quarkState_eq","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L270-L275","doc":"The quark state is the flavour shift on the unit. NOTE: it sits in word\ndegree 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.quarkLetter_order_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.quarkLetter_order_zero","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L264-L268","doc":"Order 0: a letter's `h⁰` part is its bare generator, the same for both\nflavours (flavour is invisible). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.quarkLetter_inverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.quarkLetter_inverse","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L258-L262","doc":"`σ⁻¹ = σ − h` holds in the NF algebra over `R[X]`: the two flavours of a\nletter are mutually inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.flavourShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.flavourShift","kind":"def","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L255-L256","doc":"The flavour shift: `0` for `σ`, `−1` for `σ⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.quarkState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.quarkState","kind":"def","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L252-L253","doc":"**The quark state**: the `h¹` part of a single letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.hPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.hPart","kind":"def","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L249-L250","doc":"The order-`h^k` part of an NF vector with polynomial coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.quarkLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.quarkLetter","kind":"def","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L244-L247","doc":"A single-letter quark: generator `g` (`true` = `σ₀`, `false` = `σ₁`) and\nflavour bit `ε` (`true` = `σ`, `false` = `σ⁻¹ = σ − h`), with `h` formal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.connected_eq_mulNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.connected_eq_mulNF","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L225-L230","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_eq_connected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_eq_connected","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L219-L223","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.connected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.connected","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L213-L217","doc":"The connected part `NF((γ(φ)−1)(γ(ψ)−1))` — explicit, homogeneous\nbilinear in `(φ, ψ)` — and `NF(γγ) = γ(φ) + γ(ψ) − 1 + connected`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.degPos_not_bilinear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.degPos_not_bilinear","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L206-L211","doc":"**Requirement (3) fails as stated**: with `φ = 0` the degree ≥ 1 part of\n`NF(γγ)` is `ψ`'s own polarization, not `0`; a bilinear form vanishes at\n`φ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.degPos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.degPos","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L203-L204","doc":"The word-degree ≥ 1 part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.flavour_reaches_deg0_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.flavour_reaches_deg0_witness","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L196-L201","doc":"The witness: a horizontal photon `ψ = σ₀` against the bare core. The\ndegree-0 coordinate moves by exactly `−h`, so \"word degree 0 carries no\nflavour\" fails whenever `h ≠ 0` (scope (a): true only modulo `h`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.flavour_reaches_deg0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.flavour_reaches_deg0","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L188-L194","doc":"**Flavour reaches word degree 0 at order `h¹`.** Flipping `ψ`'s letters\nmoves the degree-0 coordinate by `h·(h ψ₀₁ − φ₀ψ₀₁ − φ₁ψ₀₁ − ψ₀ − ψ₁)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.photonBar_order_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.photonBar_order_zero","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L182-L186","doc":"Flavour is invisible at order zero: at `h = 0` the flipped photon IS the\nphoton. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_deg0_h_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_deg0_h_free","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L177-L180","doc":"**Word degree 0 is `h`-free** on the γγ product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.N1_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.N1_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L173-L175","doc":"The order-1 part is not zero (two horizontal polarizations). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.N1_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.N1_smul","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L167-L171","doc":"… and homogeneous in each slot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.N1_bilin_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.N1_bilin_right","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L161-L165","doc":"… additive in `ψ` … ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.N1_bilin_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.N1_bilin_left","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L155-L159","doc":"The order-1 part is additive in `φ` … ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.N1_deg0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.N1_deg0","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L152-L153","doc":"The order-1 part lies in word degree ≥ 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_affine","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L145-L150","doc":"**`NF(γγ)` is exactly affine in `h`**: no `h²` term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.N1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.N1","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L141-L143","doc":"The order-`h¹` coefficient of `NF(γγ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.pairNF_eq","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L126-L139","doc":"**The γγ normal form** — reproduces table 5 of\n`trivial-knot-photon-interpretation` coordinate by coordinate (with\n`L₋ = σ₁σ₀` at index 3 and `L₊ = σ₀σ₁` at index 4). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.pairNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.pairNF","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L122-L124","doc":"`NF(γ(φ)·γ(ψ))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.photonBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.photonBar","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L116-L120","doc":"The flavour-flipped photon: every letter `σᵢ` replaced by\n`σᵢ⁻¹ = σᵢ − h` (the sign bit of `quark_template`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.photon_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.photon_eq","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L112-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.photon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.photon","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L107-L110","doc":"The photon with colour content: `γ(φ) = 1 + φ₀σ₀ + φ₁σ₁ + φ₀₁σ₀σ₁`,\nbuilt with the algebra product (no basis label is trusted). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.s1_mul_s0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.s1_mul_s0","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L104-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.s0_mul_s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.s0_mul_s1","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L98-L102","doc":"The basis labels are DERIVED, not asserted: `σ₀·σ₁` is coordinate 4.\n(Trap: `MarkovTraceOnHecke` labels coordinate 3 `L₊` although it is `σ₁σ₀`,\nwhile `rem:knot-basis-color-content` writes `L₊ = σ₀σ₁`, i.e. coordinate 4.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.s1","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L95-L96","doc":"`σ₁` as an NF vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.s0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.s0","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L93-L94","doc":"`σ₀` as an NF vector on the basis `[1, σ₀, σ₁, σ₁σ₀, σ₀σ₁, σ₀σ₁σ₀]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.e0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.e0","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/PhotonPairNormalForm.lean#L89-L91","doc":"The unit `1` as an NF vector (local copy of `HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.unitNF`,\nkept local so this file's import cone is `MarkovTraceOnHecke` + Mathlib). ","signatureChunk":0}]}